            <ArticleTitle>Value of preprocedure multislice computed tomographic coronary angiography to predict the outcome of percutaneous recanalization of chronic total occlusions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>240-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We performed multislice computed tomographic coronary angiography in 45 patients who had chronic total occlusions and were scheduled for percutaneous recanalization. Multivariate analysis identified a blunt stump (by conventional angiography), occlusion length &gt;15 mm, and severe calcification (by multislice computed tomographic coronary angiography) as independent predictors of procedural failure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
